te description of how many people behave under the actual conditions of prison labor as currently structured. That doesn't necessarily mean it's fixed human nature — it may partly be a rational response to a system that gives people little reason to invest. Whether changing the structure would actually shift behavior in a way that matters practically (for safety, program cost, officer workload) is a separate, harder question — and your uncle's skepticism about that is worth taking seriously too.
